        "original_id": "ae64111f-835d-50f7-93a1-fff2c67f89a8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Christopher Buckley, William F. Buckley Jr., Patricia Buckley, William Frank Buckley Sr.\n- Organizations: National Review\n- Products: Firing Line\n- Roles: writer, socialite, author, humorist\n\nFacts:\n- In 1955, William F. Buckley Jr. founded National Review magazine, which had a major impact on stimulating the conservative movement.\n- From 1966 to 1999, William F. Buckley Jr. hosted 1,429 episodes of the television show Firing Line and became known there for his transatlantic accent and wide vocabulary.\n- William F. Buckley Jr. wrote a nationally syndicated newspaper column and numerous spy novels.\n- Christopher Buckley is the son of writer William F. Buckley Jr. and socialite Patricia Buckley.\n- William Frank Buckley Sr. was the grandfather of Christopher Buckley, an author and humorist.",
